# =============================================================================
# project-squirrel -- station.env.example (issue #302, epic #212)
#
# The station env contract: EVERY external fact a standalone Aviary station
# needs, in one file. A station is a box that has never heard of this house --
# no pearl, no Pi-hole, no 192.168.1.x -- so anything the stack can't derive
# arrives here and nowhere else.
#
# Deploy: copy to /home/todd/station.env (uncommitted -- it carries an API
# key), fill in the per-station values, and let every station unit load it
# via `EnvironmentFile=/home/todd/station.env` (unit files in
# Servers/Birdhouse.md). Phase 5 (the next station) is: copy this file, edit
# the four per-station values (name, coordinates, weather location, key),
# done.
#
# SYSTEMD SYNTAX, NOT SHELL: only systemd's EnvironmentFile reader parses
# this file. Never bash-source it -- an apostrophe in any comment (there are
# several) opens an unterminated string, so `set -a; . station.env` dies on
# a syntax error (bit live 2026-08-08). To hand-run a command with these
# values, let systemd do the parsing:
#   sudo systemd-run --pipe -p EnvironmentFile=/home/todd/station.env <cmd>
# -- or export just the variables the command actually reads.
#
# The no-default philosophy travels with the box: bus.py raises without
# MERLE_MQTT, earl.py without MERLE_LATLON, willard without MERLE_OWM_KEY --
# a misconfigured station must fail at startup, never look healthy while
# publishing into the void two hours from the nearest keyboard.
# =============================================================================

# --- Identity ----------------------------------------------------------------

# The station's name, house convention (epic #212 D5). Not read by any unit
# today -- the porch masthead lives in the deployed tiles.station.json copy,
# and clip paths/source labels come from the feed name -- but the Phase 3
# sync courier will stamp every pushed digest with it, so it is part of the
# contract from day one. Lowercase, hostname-safe.
MERLE_STATION_ID=birdhouse

# Display branding for the Aviary UI (read at request time by mcc-dashboard;
# restart the dashboard after changing). Subtitle under the H1:
#MERLE_STATION_NAME=Karen's Yard
# Optional H1 override (default "The Aviary"):
#MERLE_AVIARY_TITLE=Karen's Aviary

# --- The bus (localhost by principle 1) --------------------------------------

# A station is fully self-contained: its broker is its own mosquitto on
# loopback (plus the :9001 websockets listener for the porch lamps --
# Servers/Birdhouse.md). Never a remote broker; the dashboard must work with
# the internet down.
MERLE_MQTT=localhost:1883

# --- Where the station is (the region mask + the record) ---------------------

# Latitude,longitude of the yard the mic listens to. Earl feeds it to
# BirdNET's geo model (the mandatory D4 region mask -- what makes the box
# the expert on ITS yard), and sightings seeds location 1 (Home) from it.
# Karen's box gets Portage's coordinates on deployment day; the mask
# re-localizes on the next restart.
MERLE_LATLON=42.29,-85.59

# Field Mode's start form pre-fills from MERLE_FIELD_LATLON, falling back to
# MERLE_LATLON above -- so the rover needs this set only if its default should
# differ from the station's yard (issue #384). Same "lat,lon" format.
#MERLE_FIELD_LATLON=42.29,-85.59

# --- Weather (OWM-only station mode, #301) -----------------------------------

# No MERLE_ECOWITT here, and that absence is the switch: without a gateway
# configured Willard runs OWM-only station mode -- current conditions
# (including wind, so Earl's wind rule gets a real number) from the /weather
# call at the 10-minute cadence, instrument-only fields honestly absent.
# Do NOT add MERLE_ECOWITT to a station env unless the station grows its own
# gateway; at home its absence is a misconfiguration, on a station it's the
# design.
MERLE_OWM_KEY=paste-the-openweather-key-here

# The station's location for OWM: zip, zip,CC, or lat,lon.
MERLE_WEATHER_LOC=49024,US

# Willard's seasonal archive + the dashboard's /weather/history route read
# the same file, so the path is absolute and BOTH units carry it (the
# two-WorkingDirectories lesson, Servers/Pearl.md).
MERLE_WEATHER_DB=/home/todd/project-squirrel/weather.db

# --- Earl on a no-AVX box (#299, #300) ---------------------------------------

# Stock TF wheels SIGILL on Atom-class x86 (the J5005 has no AVX). litert
# runs both birdnet.load() sites on ai-edge-litert at the same measured
# speed. Leave set on every station of this class; pearl leaves it unset.
MERLE_BIRDNET_LIBRARY=litert

# The YAMNet speech gate's LiteRT arm -- the tflite classification variant,
# fetched once at bootstrap (Servers/Birdhouse.md; ~4.1 MB, labels ride
# inside the file). Without it Earl runs UNGATED and loud, which breaks the
# epic's speech invariant -- on a station this var is load-bearing, not an
# optimization.
MERLE_YAMNET_TFLITE=/home/todd/yamnet.tflite

# --- The bird record ---------------------------------------------------------

# earl.db is the station's irreplaceable file: the life list's first-heard
# dates cannot be re-derived. Absolute path, carried by earl-sightings AND
# mcc-dashboard (the routes read what the consumer writes).
MERLE_EARL_DB=/home/todd/project-squirrel/earl.db

# The clip tree: visit recordings, the species portrait shelf. Absolute,
# carried by earl-listener, earl-sightings, and mcc-dashboard.
MERLE_EARL_CLIPS=/srv/media-cache/earl

# Clip retention (optional; default 90). Lifers' first clips are exempt
# forever either way.
#MERLE_EARL_CLIPS_KEEP_DAYS=90

# The disk budget (#330) -- the control that actually protects the volume,
# because age cannot protect a volume it does not measure. Pearl proved it:
# ~1 GB/day of clips-plus-siblings would fill its LV in a month and never
# reach the 90-day horizon. Oldest-first eviction, lifer first-clips never
# touched, portraits counted but never evicted, and every eviction logged.
# 40 GB on the station's 119 GiB SSD leaves ample room for the OS, the
# venvs, the models, and earl.db.
MERLE_EARL_CLIPS_CAP_GB=40

# --- The deploy watcher (#303) -----------------------------------------------

# The release channel (#354). Stations never ride raw main: this branch is
# fast-forwarded to main's tip once nightly (~2 AM Eastern, the
# promote-stations GitHub Action), so builds land while the house sleeps and
# the box absorbs at most a day of changes per deploy. The env knob is HALF
# the flip -- the checkout must actually sit on the branch (git fetch &&
# git checkout aviary-station-stable), then restart station-autodeploy; a
# station checkout left on main reads as pinned and deploys nothing. Pearl
# and merle never set this (the script's default is main).
MERLE_DEPLOY_BRANCH=aviary-station-stable

# The units station-autodeploy restarts on any deploy (the channel moving,
# for a station). The role's
# unit list lives HERE -- in the profile, not in the script and not in a
# hand-edited unit file -- so the watcher consumes the same contract as
# everything else. Quotes required: the value has spaces and systemd's
# EnvironmentFile honors them.
MERLE_DEPLOY_UNITS="earl-listener earl-sightings willard-weather earl-enrichment"

# Rebuild + restart the dashboard when a merge touches mcc/ (the
# deploy-mcc.sh order: install -> build -> restart; a failed build never
# restarts, old code keeps serving). Every station serves the MCC, so this
# is 1 on every station.
MERLE_DEPLOY_MCC=1

# --- Enrichment: portraits yes, field notes no (#312) ------------------------

# The enrichment loop runs on a station in PROFILE-ONLY mode: the Wikipedia
# pass (stdlib HTTP, no model) dresses every new lifer with a portrait and a
# description within a tick, and the field-notes pass is a no-op because
# MERLE_OLLAMA is unset -- the loop says so at startup ("ollama candidates:
# none (profile pass only)").
#
# This 0 is belt-and-braces, not the mechanism: unset MERLE_OLLAMA already
# means no notes. It documents the intent at the config layer so that adding
# a model host later is a deliberate decision about cost and CPU, never a
# side effect. (The hosted-model species analysis is epic #212's
# post-birthday addition and arrives with its own env.)
MERLE_ENRICH_CAP=0

# Tick every 5 minutes rather than the code's 15 (default 900). The 900
# was priced for PEARL's tick, where a turn of the crank can drain field
# notes through Ollama -- 1-2 minutes of CPU per species on a workstation
# someone is sitting at. On a station that cost is structurally zero (no
# model, CAP=0), so the only work a tick can do is the Wikipedia pass.
#
# This does NOT increase load on Wikipedia: a species with no usable page
# is retried ~daily by the profile_attempts stamps regardless of tick
# rate, and THROTTLE_S spaces out a burst. A quiet tick is a couple of SQL
# queries against a small local DB.
#
# What it buys: the loop ticks once at startup, so a new lifer's wait is
# random within the interval -- average 7.5 min becomes 2.5 min. That is
# the difference between hearing a new bird, opening the page, and finding
# it already dressed, versus finding it blank. Worth most in the first
# days, when every bird is a lifer.
MERLE_ENRICH_INTERVAL_S=300

# --- What must NOT be set on a station ---------------------------------------

# MERLE_ECOWITT -- see the weather section above: its absence IS station mode.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MERLE_MQTT_WS -- a BUILD-time var (mcc/.env.local at home, never
# this file): Next inlines it into the JS bundle, and busUrl() falls back to
# ws://<page-host>:9001 when it's unset, which is exactly right on a station.
# Never copy pearl's mcc/.env.local onto a station -- the build would bake
# pearl's LAN address into every page, the lamps would go dark, and no
# runtime env could fix it (rebuild required).
#
# MERLE_OLLAMA -- no LLM on a J5005; the hosted-model species analysis is the
# epic's post-birthday addition and arrives with its own env when it ships.
#
# MERLE_DAEMON_URL -- there is no perception daemon in a station's life; the
# dashboard treats daemon-down as a normal state by design.

# --- The feed registry -------------------------------------------------------

# Points Earl at the STATION registry (the local window mic) instead of the
# committed feeds.yml, which describes this house's cameras and rover. The
# committed feeds.station.yml serves every station unedited; see its header
# before touching the device name.
MERLE_FEEDS=/home/todd/project-squirrel/feeds.station.yml
